            "review_title": "Review at Papa's Chicken",
            "review_text": "Nick M\nHanoi, Vietnam15 contributions\n0\nIn short, dreadful\nJun 2020\nWhilst enjoying an evening with two of my close friends, we came to the mutual decision to have some succulent and tender chicken delivered. With hearts racing and anticipation growing, our order arrived in acceptable time. 3 boxes of chicken. Chicken by name, but not by nature - I'll tell you that for free. This \"chicken\" had either passed through a wake of vultures (just to make my point abundantly clear, a \"wake\" is the collective name of vultures feeding by the way) and had all meat stripped off the bone, or you need to consider a name change - hint: if you're not actually going to serve chicken with meat, remove the \"chicken\" from your name Papa! \nIf my friend Kimodo (false name to protect her identity - she doesn't need the fame whilst she's working hard on starting her business) hadn't then gone and rustled up a prawn paella, there's a chance I would have wasted away overnight and perished. \nIf you think I'll be ordering again from your Papa, you've got another thing coming. Good day!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 17, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
